1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,577
Day 53: CLI Agent Orchestrator,

2
00:00:02,577 --> 00:00:06,568
AWS's framework for coordinating AI coding CLIs,

3
00:00:06,568 --> 00:00:10,310
with Claude Code handing work to Claude Code.

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,560
CAO runs a local server,

5
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:16,910
starts each agent as a real command line tool inside tmux,

6
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:20,210
and lets a supervisor hand tasks to workers.

7
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:24,015
A launch command asks the local server for a new session.

8
00:00:24,465 --> 00:00:26,778
The server opens a tmux pane and

9
00:00:26,778 --> 00:00:29,452
starts Claude Code as the supervisor.

10
00:00:29,452 --> 00:00:32,198
It can read files, but not write them.

11
00:00:32,648 --> 00:00:35,492
So the supervisor opens a second pane and

12
00:00:35,492 --> 00:00:38,058
hands the task to a developer worker.

13
00:00:38,508 --> 00:00:41,473
The worker writes both files, reports back,

14
00:00:41,473 --> 00:00:43,059
and its pane is closed.

15
00:00:43,509 --> 00:00:45,130
The first runs timed out.

16
00:00:45,130 --> 00:00:47,400
CAO looks for the words Welcome to,

17
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,864
matched Ubuntu's login banner instead,

18
00:00:49,864 --> 00:00:52,653
and never answered the folder trust prompt.

19
00:00:52,653 --> 00:00:55,052
Once we trusted the folder ourselves,

20
00:00:55,052 --> 00:00:57,905
the handoff finished in forty seven seconds.

21
00:00:58,355 --> 00:01:02,201
The full write-up, including a settings change CAO makes to

22
00:01:02,201 --> 00:01:03,766
Claude Code, is on Zenn.
